CharacterizationRule.Notes:
This is a source for a control in SAPUI5. This is effectively a new HTML tag that can be used in either a view
or code. Effectively anything can be passed to it, which means it's effectively like a library function. 

Therefore we want a generic source to say that anything retrieved _could_ be user-controlled.

The code is typically of the form:

sap.ui.define([
    "sap/ui/core/Control"
], function (Control) {
    return Control.extend("CustomControl", {
        metadata: {
            properties: {
                foo: { type: "string", defaultValue: "" }
            }
        },
        renderer: {
            render: function (oRm, oControl) {
                // [RuleTest] Cross-Site Scripting: SAPUI5 Control
                oRm.write("<div>" + oControl.getId() + ":" + oControl.getFoo() + "</div>"); // get[A-Z][A-z]+
                // [RuleTest]! Cross-Site Scripting: SAPUI5 Control
                oRm.writeEscaped("<div><p>Escaped: " + oControl.getId() + ":" + oControl.getFoo() + "</p></div>");
                try {
                    // [RuleTest] Dynamic Code Evaluation: Code Injection
                    eval(oControl.getFoo())
                } catch { }
            }
        },
        init: function () { }
    })
})

This means that you're extending an existing control and the renderer takes a RenderManager and the Control you're extending (in this case the base Control object).
So any getter on oControl could theoretically be user-controlled as it's just a control to be used anywhere within the application and to be passed any (potentially
user-controlled) data.

CharacterizationRule.StructuralMatch:
FunctionCall fc: 
    fc.possibleTargets contains [Function:
        /* since a control is a library function, basically anything can be a source of taint. All properties are of the form getFoo */
        name matches "get[A-Z][A-z0-9]*" 
        /* getId is always on controls and would lead to FPs as is very unlikely user-controlled, so is excluded */
        and not name == "getId"
    ]*
    and fc.instance is [Expression e: 
        /* in 21.2, SCA understands that the SAPUI5 object chain with regard to controls, so the supers should contain Control */
        possibleTypes contains [Type: definition.supers contains [Class: name == "Control"]]
    ]
    and enclosingFunction is [Function f: parameters.length == 2 and f.name matches "render(er)?"]

