CharacterizationRule.Notes:
SIL sink for location.href.

For AngularJS $location.href = value is legacy, and is now done by $location.path(value);
Although the latter doesn't seem to be exploitable.

CharacterizationRule.StructuralMatch:
AccessLocation al: al.accessName == "href" and
    al.accessInstance is [Location: name matches "(\$)?location"]
    and al in [AssignmentStatement:
        lhs.location is [Location l:
            l.transitiveBase === al.transitiveBase
        ]
        and not rhs is [AccessLocation:
            accessName == "href"
            and accessInstance is [Location:
                name == "location"
                or possibleTypes contains [Type: name == "Location"]
            ]
        ]
        /* check contains in case of inside operation */
        and not rhs contains [AccessLocation:
            accessName == "href"
            and accessInstance is [Location:
                name == "location"
                or possibleTypes contains [Type: name == "Location"]
            ]
        ]
        and not rhs is [Location:
            name == "$location"
            or possibleTypes contains [Type: name == "Location"]
        ]
        /* check contains in case of inside operation */
        and not rhs contains [Location:
            name == "$location"
            or possibleTypes contains [Type: name == "Location"]
        ]
    ]

